    },
    "interpretation": "The 2003 article by Guo Hongjie explicitly associates the 1939 building at no. 9 with its then-current conversion. The 2022 closing account documents an archival exhibition building open 2004–January 2022. Archived 2006 reporting counts eleven usable floors and 9,270 m² after refurbishment. The heritage description counts twelve levels at the central mass and two fewer at the edges. Neither value is used to infer a measured roof height. Dates 1937–February 1939 describe the extant building, distinct from the earlier shipping compound on the French Bund; the 2025 Xinhua account addresses this longer history."
  },
